    <innerclass refid="classOpenSkyhawk_1_1Pdu_1_1TelemSchedule" prot="public">OpenSkyhawk::Pdu::TelemSchedule</innerclass>
    <innernamespace refid="namespaceOpenSkyhawk">OpenSkyhawk</innernamespace>
    <innernamespace refid="namespaceOpenSkyhawk_1_1Pdu">OpenSkyhawk::Pdu</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>When to send which TELEM_n page — periodic rotation plus rate-limited edge sends (#216). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Periodic: one frame per TELEM_PERIOD_MS (the HEALTH_n rate), rotating through the pages, so each page refreshes every PAGES × period. A periodic send is the one that restarts that page&apos;s statistics window.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Edge: when a page&apos;s flag byte differs from what was last sent for it, send that page now — at most once per EDGE_MIN_MS per page; a change inside the hold-off goes out when it ends. An edge send does not restart the window. Every page starts from an all-clear baseline (0), so a condition present at boot goes out promptly instead of waiting for its periodic slot.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Hardware-free — the caller supplies the clock and the current flag bytes.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="copyright"><para>GPL-2.0-only — see Firmware/LICENSE </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
